.SH NAME
sdrwatch \- SDR non\-volatile data store activity monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBsdrwatch\fR \fIsdr_name\fR [ \-t | \-s | \-r | \-z ] [\fIinterval\fR [\fIcount\fR [ verbose ]]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
For \fIcount\fR interations (defaulting to 1), \fBsdrwatch\fR sleeps \fIinterval\fR
seconds and then performs the SDR operation indicated by the specified
mode: 's' to print statistics, 'r' to reset statistics, 'z' to print ZCO
space utilization, 't' (the default) to call the \fBsdr_print_trace()\fR function
(see \fBsdr\fR\|(3)) to report on SDR data storage management activity in the SDR
data store identified by \fIsdr_name\fR during that interval.  If the optional
\&\fBverbose\fR parameter is specified, the printed SDR activity trace will be
verbose as described in \fBsdr\fR\|(3).
.PP
If \fIinterval\fR is zero, \fBsdrwatch\fR just performs the indicated operation
once (for 't', it merely prints a current usage summary for the indicated
data store) and terminates.
.PP
\&\fBsdrwatch\fR is helpful for detecting and diagnosing storage space leaks.  For
debugging the ION protocol stack, \fIsdr_name\fR is normally "ion" but might be
overridden by the value of sdrName in the .ionconfig file used to configure
the node under study.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.IX Header "EXIT STATUS"
.IP """0""" 4
.IX Item """0"""
\&\fBsdrwatch\fR has terminated.
.SH FILES
.IX Header "FILES"
No configuration files are needed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.IX Header "ENVIRONMENT"
No environment variables apply.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.IX Header "DIAGNOSTICS"
The following diagnostics may be issued to the \fBion.log\fR log file:
.IP "Can't attach to sdr." 4
.IX Item "Can't attach to sdr."
ION system error.  One possible cause is that ION has not yet been
initialized on the local computer; run \fBionadmin\fR\|(1) to correct this.
.IP "Can't start trace." 4
.IX Item "Can't start trace."
Insufficient ION working memory to contain trace information.  Reinitialize
ION with more memory.
.SH BUGS
.IX Header "BUGS"
Report bugs to <https://github.com/nasa\-jpl/ION\-DTN/issues>
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBsdr\fR\|(3), \fBpsmwatch\fR\|(1)
